-   - **Compile every code sample** against the declared `targets` before you save the topic, as [agents/writing-opinions.md](../../agents/writing-opinions.md) asks of an opinion. Under the sample, record the SDK, the package versions, and the date you compiled it. For a fragment that can't compile alone, compile the smallest complete example that hosts it, and say so. CI doesn't compile research, so a sample you didn't build reaches `resolve-research` unchecked.
-   - **Check every package the topic recommends for security advisories** at the version it names. Run `<id> list package --vulnerable` in the project you compiled the samples in, or look the package up in the [GitHub Advisory Database](https://github.com/advisories). Record the date, and if an advisory is open, say so in the topic.
+   - **Compile every code example** on the declared `targets` before you save the topic, as [agents/writing-opinions.md](../../agents/writing-opinions.md) asks of an opinion: it passes `CARGO_BUILD_WARNINGS=deny cargo check` and `CARGO_BUILD_WARNINGS=deny cargo clippy`. Under the example, record the toolchain, the crate versions, and the date you compiled it. For a fragment that can't compile alone, compile the smallest complete example that hosts it, and say so. CI doesn't compile research, so an example you didn't build reaches `resolve-research` unchecked.
+   - **Check every crate the topic recommends for security advisories** at the version it names. Run `cargo deny check advisories` in a project whose `Cargo.lock` resolves the crate to that version, such as the one you compiled the examples in, or look the crate up in the [<name>Sec Advisory Database](https://rustsec.org/). Record the date, and if an advisory is open, say so in the topic.
